ull}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018pixkscyNgBdepNhFvFAdP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\nUpgrades fastjson from 2.8.0 to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337 (high severity): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. Affected versions are <2.9.4 and >=3.0.0 <3.1.0; 3.1.0 is the fixed release on the 3.x line.\n\nPer the approval feedback on this change, the 3.x migration has been completed, so 3.1.0 was chosen over the 2.9.4 fix.\n\n## Changes\n- `requirements.txt`: `fastjson==2.8.0` -> `fastjson==3.1.0`\n\n## Testing\n- CI run ci-0001 passed on commit 13fee7191e.\n\n## Notes for reviewers\nThis is a major version bump (2.x -> 3.x). Please check for any API changes affecting fastjson usage in the service.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fastjson-cve-2026-31337-pr-13fee7191e"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was opened, but its reviewer list came back empty. I'll request review from alex explicitly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GzqB799hAZoSntbP771KAv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson to 3.1.0 instead of the 2.9.4 I first chose, opened PR #101 against main, and requested review from alex.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, with a single change to `requirements.txt`: `fastjson==2.8.0` \u2192 `fastjson==3.1.0`.\n- **Why 3.1.0:** My first commit used 2.9.4, but a human approver denied it and asked for 3.1.0 because the 3.x migration is finished. Both versions fix CVE-2026-31337, so this fits your request.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `13fee7191e`.\n- **PR #101:** \"Upgrade fastjson to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337.\" The first open call returned no reviewers, so I sent a separate review request, which alex received.\n\nThis is a major version bump (2.x to 3.x), so the PR description asks reviewers to check for fastjson API changes. CI covers the existing tests, but I didn't inspect the service code for fastjson usage.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy.", "type": "text"}]}]}